notes               = "Untitled in source. The closing line condenses one the poet had already written at length: shelter-wall (page 60) has و در فاصله دو انفجار / به دیدار تو میشتابم — 'and in the space between two explosions I hurry to see you'. Here the same interval becomes the whole account of how he writes, addressed to his wife. Not a duplicate of that poem: five lines, different poem, self-quotation. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

به همسرم گفتم...
با من مهربان نباش...
من همیشه شعرم را...
در فاصلهٔ دو انفجار گفته‌ام...
آذر ۱۳۶۸

===machine===

I said to my wife...
Don't be kind to me...
I have always spoken my poem...
in the space between two explosions...
Azar 1368

===lantern===

I said to my wife...
Don't be kind to me...
I have always said my poem
in the space between two explosions...

Azar 1368

